# sandboxed-devenv backend: copied to /home/dev/.ssh/config
# One file per repository under config.d/, written by `backend repo add`: an alias
# `Host github.com-<owner>-<repo>` bound to that repository's deploy key with IdentitiesOnly,
# and the checkout's remote uses the alias (PLAN.md, "Projects and repositories").
Include config.d/*.conf
# No agent, ever: the IDE backend offers git an agent socket that proxies to the client, and
# OpenSSH asks any agent about the configured identity even with IdentitiesOnly. That query
# alone makes the client show its "Provide SSH Key Access" dialog (seen 9 October 2026).
# Nothing in this VM may fetch keys from the client.
Host *
    ForwardAgent no
    IdentityAgent none
